{greeting}

I'm {rep_first} with Project One Roofing, a local roofer here in Northern Colorado. We're doing free roof inspections in {city} this month.

{storm_hook}

It takes about 20 minutes. You get photos of anything we find and a straight answer on whether there's damage worth an insurance claim - or whether the roof is fine.

Would a day this week work for a quick look?

{greeting}

A quick follow-up on the free inspection. Hail usually bruises shingles and dents vents and gutters in ways you can't see from the ground, and insurance claims have a filing window.

If you'd like a look, reply with a day that works and I'll confirm a time. If now's not the time, no problem at all.

{greeting}

I won't keep emailing. If a storm ever has you wondering about your roof, reply to this email or call and I'll come take a look - there's never a charge for an inspection.

Take care.

{greeting}

With the recent storm in {city}, I wanted to offer a free check on your roof. It takes about 20 minutes, and catching damage early keeps a small repair from turning into a bigger one.

Reply with a day that works and I'll confirm a time.
